{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>Sulfur and salt, the entire land was burned.</b> What does salt have to do with sulfur? Rather, there is nothing that withstands fire more than salt, and there is nothing consumed by fire more than sulfur. This tells you: if they had fulfilled the Torah, they would have stood firm like salt, which fire does not consume. Now that they did not fulfill it, the fire that the Torah issues from shall consume them like sulfur, which fire does consume." "<b>And salt.</b> As it is written, 'and she became a pillar of salt.'" "<b>The entire land was burned.</b> Would HaShem be angered at the entire congregation over the sin of an individual? There is a reply to this: the idol of Michah, whose roots grew — after it the tribe of Dan strayed, and after it the ten tribes."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:54:45.588121160Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}